# NX789J system-boot diagnostics -> raw rawdump partition. REMOVE once it boots.
#
# Lives on /system_ext, not /vendor, since build 17: the port is being tested
# both with a vendor image built from extracted blobs AND with the untouched
# stock vendor partition (the approach the RedMagic 11 Pro / NX809J LineageOS
# port boots with). Anything on /vendor disappears in the stock-vendor pairing,
# and this is the only window into a boot with no adb and no working pstore.
#
# The interpreter stays /vendor/bin/sh: its file label is what puts the service
# in vendor_qti_init_shell (seen in every dump so far), and that label is the
# same on both vendor images. The script itself is only read by sh.
#
# The system bootloops and there is no adb, so this is the only way to see why.
# Trigger as early as possible; the service is oneshot, first trigger wins.
service nxdiagsys /vendor/bin/sh /system_ext/bin/nx789j-diag-system.sh
    disabled
    oneshot

on early-init
    start nxdiagsys

on init
    start nxdiagsys

on post-fs
    start nxdiagsys
